      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To create authentic low-level street figures in your noir setting, consider characters like Vinnie \"The Bull\" LaRosa, a gruff but charismatic street hustler with a heart of gold, who controls a small-time network of bums and junkies. Jackie \"Jane Doe\" Valentine is a sassy, peripatetic street singer, adapting her performances to whatever dingy bar or cramped alley will pay her. Weary Henry Morse is the info-whisperer, scrapping existence as a factotum for scrap metal dealers or hastily-assembled repair services in hidden workshops.",
